{"t": 1787308654.326, "kind": "message", "args": {"text": "All 3 tests pass. \n\n**Summary of the fix:**\n\nThe bug was in `logtrim/cli.py:16` \u2014 the `parse_line_date` function used `\"%d-%b-%Y\"` (day-month-abbreviated year, e.g., `01-Aug-2026`) to parse log dates, but the logs use ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD` (e.g., `2026-01-01`). This caused `strptime` to fail silently (returning `None`), which made `stale_lines` skip all lines and report `trimmed 0 lines`.\n\n**Changed:** `logtrim/cli.py:16` \u2014 `\"%d-%b-%Y\"` \u2192 `\"%Y-%m-%d\"`"}, "raw_ref": 59}
